Let's write a Java program to find the largest element in an array efficiently.

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class MaxNumberFinder {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        int size = scanner.nextInt(); // Reading the size of the array
        int[] array = new int[size]; // Assuming the size is stored in the array

        // Reading the array elements
        for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
            array[i] = scanner.nextInt(); // Reading each element
        }

        // Initialize the largest number variable
        int largestNumber = array[0];

        // Iterate through the array to find the largest number
        for (int i = 1; i < size; i++) {
            if (array[i] > largestNumber) {
                largestNumber = array[i];
            }
        }

        // Output the largest number
        System.out.println("The largest number is: " + largestNumber);
    }
}
```

